sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Bounded task execution and result release
  accDescr: Main execution path through the authenticated host, bridge, OpenShell and DSH. Completion, execution failure or cancellation all lead to bounded owned cleanup. Unknown cleanup blocks success. Result authorization precedes return, user delivery remains the host's responsibility.
  participant H as Host application
  participant B as Harness Bridge
  participant O as OpenShell
  participant D as Existing DSH

  H->>B: execute(trusted task, signal)
  B->>H: authorizeAdmission
  H-->>B: Allow
  B->>O: Create sandbox, verify native identity
  opt Ordinary Skill supplied
    B->>O: Upload SKILL.md
  end
  B->>O: Upload DSH patch
  B->>O: Fixed headless exec, prompt on stdin
  O->>D: Start task
  D-->>O: Final text + completed event + session ID
  O-->>B: Native JSON event stream

  Note over B,O: Cleanup survives cancellation.<br/>Separate deadline: up to 60s.
  B->>O: Recheck ownership, stop, verify stopped
  B->>O: Delete, verify generated name is absent

  alt Cleanup verified
    B->>H: authorizeResult
    H-->>B: Allow or deny current result release
    B-->>H: Completed / failed, or blocked if denied
  else Cleanup uncertain
    B->>H: authorizeResult for blocked result
    B-->>H: Blocked, no successful output
  end
  Note over H,B: The host checks accounting and current audience before delivery.
